  "summary": "Reported: James O'Connor (Warehouse Supervisor, Operations, user_id 8, America/Chicago, hours 06:00-14:00) says his warehouse office desktop isn't connecting to the network. His shift starts in about an hour, so he's blocked (triage P2). Checked: account is active, not locked, sign-in not blocked. Desktop BL-DT-0108 (Windows 11 Pro, assigned to him) is OFFLINE. Last check-in 2026-10-11T00:55:07Z. Disk is fine (78% free), no device warnings. No KB covers a wired desktop with no network: KB-014 is about Wi-Fi on laptops, so I only used its basic checks. I can't fix this remotely. Still needed: diagnose the network path (switch port/patch, cable, NIC, DHCP/VLAN), check whether other devices in the warehouse office are affected (if several, this may be a wider outage and could be P1), and possibly send someone on site. I've asked the user to check the cable and link lights, restart the desktop, and tell us whether nearby colleagues are affected.",
  "reason": "Desktop offline, no KB covers a wired desktop network failure, and Tier 1 tools can't fix it. User blocked and shift starts soon."
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, I checked and your warehouse office desktop isn't connecting to our network at the moment. Your account itself is fine. I've passed this to our Tier 2 network team as urgent, since you need the desktop before your shift. While you wait, here are some quick things to try: (1) make sure the network cable is plugged in firmly at the back of the desktop and at the wall, and see if the little lights next to the port are on or blinking; (2) restart the desktop. Please also reply to let us know if anyone else nearby in the warehouse office has lost their network. That helps the team find the cause faster. If the restart fixes it, just let us know.",
  "internal_note": "Sender verified: James O'Connor, user_id 8. Account active, not locked or blocked. Device BL-DT-0108 (desktop, Win 11) is offline. Last check-in 2026-10-11T00:55:07Z. Disk is healthy and there are no warnings. No KB covers a wired desktop with no network (KB-014 is for Wi-Fi on laptops; I only used its basic checks). Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation_id 1) to diagnose the switch port, cable, NIC or DHCP and possibly send someone on site. I asked the user to check the cable and link lights, restart, and tell us if colleagues are affected. If several people are down, re-prioritize as a possible office outage (P1/P2) under KB-014's escalation criteria.",
